{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf6iu7Jt2oqPPpL9FdNqf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Error responses use sealed `ApiException` classes (ConflictException → 409, ResourceNotFoundException → 404)\n- ErrorCode enum defines machine-readable codes; all error responses must include code and message\n- Tests assert both HTTP status and error envelope structure (e.g., `jsonPath(\"$.error.code\")`)\n- In-memory repositories using ConcurrentHashMap; `save()` overwrites, `findById()` returns optional\n- Controllers throw exceptions for error cases; GlobalExceptionHandler converts them to ApiError envelopes\n\n**Affected files:**\n- `Order.kt` — must add OrderStatus enum and status field\n- `OrderRepository.kt` — no code change needed (already saves with new field)\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt` — must add `findByOrderId(orderId: String)` method to find shipments by order\n- `OrderController.kt` — must add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint\n- `ShipmentController.kt` — must reject POST /shipments if order is CANCELLED\n- `ApiError.kt` — must add ORDER_CANCELLED error code\n- `OrderControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for cancel scenarios\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add test for reject on cancelled order\n\n**Risks:**\n- All-or-nothing atomicity: cancel must fail entirely if any shipment is CONFIRMED, leaving order ACTIVE\n- Idempotency: cancelling an already-CANCELLED order must succeed without error\n- Cross-module validation: ShipmentController must check order status\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `OrderStatus` enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED states, add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order, update CreateOrderRequest. New orders will default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt**: No changes to code (the ConcurrentHashMap already persists the new field).\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method that filters shipments by orderId.\n\n4. **ApiError.kt**: Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` error code to the ErrorCode enum (new 409 condition).\n\n5. **OrderController.kt**: \n   - Inject ShipmentRepository\n   - Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n     - Finds the order; if not found, throw ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n     - If order is already CANCELLED, return it unchanged (idempotent)\n     - If any shipment is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED code (409), changing nothing\n     - Transition order to CANCELLED, cancel all CREATED shipments (update their status to CANCELLED), persist, return the order\n\n6. **ShipmentController.kt**:\n   - Inject OrderRepository\n   - In the `create` method, after checking shipmentId duplicate, check if the order exists and is CANCELLED; if so, throw ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED (409)\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests for:\n   - Cancel active order succeeds, persists, and returns cancelled order\n   - Cancel already-cancelled order succeeds without error\n   - Cancel with confirmed shipment is rejected 409, order stays ACTIVE, shipments unchanged\n   - Cancel unknown order is rejected 404\n   - GET order after cancel shows CANCELLED status\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add test for:\n   - Create shipment on cancelled order is rejected 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\n**Rejected alternative:**\nI considered using a separate `OrderService` class to handle the cancel logic, but that would add complexity without improving the single-responsibility principle here—the OrderController already orchestrates repository calls, and cancel is just another transition. Keeping it in the controller stays consistent with the existing create/get pattern.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n- **Successful cancel of ACTIVE order**:\n  - Read: Order from repository, all shipments by orderId\n  - Check: Order exists? Is any shipment CONFIRMED?\n  - Write: Order.status → CANCELLED, each CREATED shipment.status → CANCELLED\n  - Return: 200 OK with cancelled Order\n  \n- **Retry cancel of CANCELLED order**:\n  - Read: Order from repository\n  - Check: Order exists? (yes)\n  - Write: None (already CANCELLED)\n  - Return: 200 OK with Order (unchanged)\n  \n- **Cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment**:\n  - Read: Order from repository, all shipments by orderId\n  - Check: Any shipment CONFIRMED?\n  - Write: None\n  - Return: 409 ConflictException (ORDER_CANCELLED code)\n  \n- **Cancel non-existent order**:\n  - Read: Order from repository (not found)\n  - Return: 404 ResourceNotFoundException (ORDER_NOT_FOUND code)\n  \n- **Create shipment on CANCELLED order**:\n  - Read: Order from repository\n  - Check: Order exists? Is it CANCELLED?\n  - Return: 409 ConflictException (ORDER_CANCELLED code) if CANCELLED\n\n**Test strategy:**\n1. **cancel_active_order_succeeds** — POST cancel ACTIVE order → 200, order is CANCELLED, created shipments are cancelled\n2. **cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds** — POST cancel CANCELLED order → 200, no changes, idempotent\n3. **cancel_blocked_by_confirmed_shipment** — POST cancel when CONFIRMED exists → 409 ORDER_CANCELLED, order stays ACTIVE\n4. **cancel_unknown_order** — POST cancel non-existent → 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n5. **get_order_shows_cancelled_status** — After cancel, GET returns CANCELLED status\n6. **create_shipment_on_cancelled_order_rejected** — POST shipment to CANCELLED order → 409 ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. Let me start with the foundational data model changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1576,"cache_read_input_tokens":20432,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1576},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f653fa64-a0f9-442a-a7e1-e0a69e7c4d8a","uuid":"3fff59c4-169f-4542-8145-70659ae64f1b","timestamp":"2026-09-16T07:28:08.394Z","request_id":"req_011Cf6iu6ktSMJgRbucJw4Ri"}
