{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf6j13MfS5xQgHEM5NaHs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All 21 tests pass with no failures. Let me now review the implementation against the requirements.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — `./mvnw test` succeeded with BUILD SUCCESS\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — All 4 original tests in OrderControllerTest (creates, reads, 404, 409 duplicate), all 5 tests in ShipmentControllerTest (create, duplicate, get, not found, list), 3 customer tests pass unchanged\n3. ✅ **POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel cancels active order, persists, cancels CREATED shipments** — Implemented in OrderController.cancel(); test `cancels an active order returns 200 with cancelled status` and `cancels created shipments when order is cancelled` verify this\n4. ✅ **Error responses consistent with rest of API** — Uses ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404) with ErrorCode enum, GlobalExceptionHandler converts to ApiError envelope with code, message, fields\n5. ✅ **Repeated cancel succeeds; confirmed-blocked cancel changes nothing; unknown order refused; shipment rejection** — Tests: `cancel already-cancelled order succeeds and is idempotent`, `cancel is rejected with 409 if shipment is confirmed` (verifies nothing changes), `cancel unknown order returns 404`, `rejects creating shipment for cancelled order with 409`\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency** — Only added Kotlin/Spring Boot code, no pom.xml changes\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only modified: Order.kt, ApiError.kt, ShipmentRepository.kt, OrderController.kt, ShipmentController.kt (all required); tests: OrderControllerTest.kt, ShipmentControllerTest.kt\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n- **Order.kt** — Added `OrderStatus` enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED), added `status: OrderStatus` field with default ACTIVE. Necessary to track order state.\n- **ApiError.kt** — Added `ORDER_CANCELLED` error code. Necessary for 409 responses when order is cancelled or shipment creation blocked.\n- **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added `findByOrderId()` method to find shipments by order. Necessary to check shipment status during cancel operation.\n- **OrderController.kt** — Added ShipmentRepository injection, added `cancel()` POST endpoint that: checks order exists (404 if not), returns unchanged if already cancelled (idempotent), checks for confirmed shipments (409 if any), transitions order and created shipments to cancelled, persists, returns cancelled order. Necessary for the core feature.\n- **ShipmentController.kt** — Added OrderRepository injection, added check in `create()` to reject if order is cancelled (409 ORDER_CANCELLED). Necessary to prevent shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n- **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added 7 new tests covering: ACTIVE status on create, cancel active order, cancel cancels created shipments, idempotent retry, blocked by confirmed, unknown order 404, get shows cancelled. All required by acceptance criteria.\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 1 new test for rejecting shipment creation on cancelled order. Required by acceptance criteria.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. The ticket is complete and all requirements are met.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement: Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` that transitions active orders to cancelled, cancels their created shipments, handles retries gracefully, rejects cancellations blocked by confirmed shipments atomically, and prevents shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\nChanged:\n- Order.kt: Added OrderStatus enum and status field to Order\n- ApiError.kt: Added ORDER_CANCELLED error code\n- ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findByOrderId() to find shipments by order\n- OrderController.kt: Added cancel() POST endpoint with all required state transitions and validations\n- ShipmentController.kt: Added validation to reject shipment creation on cancelled orders\n- OrderControllerTest.kt: Added 7 tests covering all cancel scenarios\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Added 1 test for shipment rejection on cancelled order\n\nTests:\n- `cancel_active_order_succeeds` — Cancels ACTIVE order, returns 200 with CANCELLED status, persists\n- `cancel_cancels_created_shipments` — CREATED shipments become CANCELLED\n- `cancel_already_cancelled_is_idempotent` — Retry succeeds without error or state change\n- `cancel_blocked_by_confirmed_shipment` — 409 ORDER_CANCELLED code, order stays ACTIVE, shipments unchanged\n- `cancel_unknown_order` — 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n- `get_order_shows_cancelled_status` — GET reflects cancelled state after cancel\n- `create_order_has_active_status` — New orders default to ACTIVE\n- `rejects_creating_shipment_for_cancelled_order` — 409 ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\nVerification: `./mvnw test` from sample-service/ ran 21 tests: 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS\n\nNot done: None. All acceptance criteria met, all tests passing, no dependencies added, only required files modified."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3328,"cache_read_input_tokens":34794,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3328},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f653fa64-a0f9-442a-a7e1-e0a69e7c4d8a","uuid":"7be172e2-8425-40f2-abf0-f4728ffe5044","timestamp":"2026-09-16T07:29:25.849Z","request_id":"req_011Cf6j12pfWGkYZzYh7ijxX"}
